    "ruling": "Maintainer, 2026-10-19: there is one class. The typing identifies large groups of cells from identifying features that are mutually exclusive by a priori knowledge, then uses the full marker set in targeted ways inside each group; the broad and refined designations are steps to the same result. Each table's class_column holds that result, and no second class column is carried.",
    "tables": {
      "pancreas": {
        "tissue": "pancreas",
        "class_column": "refined_class",
        "within": {
          "Immune": [
            "immune_class",
            "immune_subtype"
          ]
        },
        "carry": [
          "excluded_reason",
          "endocrine_object_id",
          "endocrine_object_class",
          "islet_key",
          "islet_route",
          "islet_stratum",
          "producer"
        ],
        "not_a_class": [
          "Excluded"
        ],
        "exposed": {
          "immune_subtype": "T-CD8 and T-CD4-helper set CD8 against CD4 in one cell. UniFORM's factors are per marker, so on these four donors CD8 is multiplied 3.7-19x as much as CD4; a within-donor step is not ruled (delivery README, 2026-10-19)."
        }
      },
      "nodes": {
        "tissue": "pLN",
        "class_column": "immune_class",
        "within": {
          "T_cell": [
            "t_nk_class"
          ]
        },
        "carry": [
          "is_immune",
          "typing_status",
          "stage2_reason",
          "pln_annotation_id",
          "block_relationship",
          "producer"
        ],
        "not_a_class": [
          "",
          "Uncalled"
        ],
        "ruling": "Maintainer, 2026-10-19: 'pLN is not a class it is a tissue that needs to have cell typing done based on the lymph node cell types in the phenotyping spreadsheets for lymph node', and later the same day: 'typing needs to happen for all cells so for cells that exist in both pancreas and lymph node, use the pancreas typing methods.' Delivered so far: build_pln_immune_pheno.py, which 'types immune cells using the lineage marker sets (core/phenocycler/scripts/typing/lineages.py:23) and shared identity panels' (core/panels/data/identity_core), run on the workstation for these four donors. It names immune lineages only, so it is not the finished node typing: every node cell is to be typed, the cell types the node shares with the pancreas by the pancreas typing methods (HANDOFF_2026-10-19.md, item D). Until that arrives the lane carries this table in the pancreas's shape: the lineage immune_class (T_cell, Myeloid, B_Plasma, Granulocyte), with the T/NK subset t_nk_class carried inside T_cell. Not a class: the producer's empty label, on a cell whose cluster read structural (is_immune false) or named no lineage (is_immune null), and Uncalled, an immune cell that no subpanel named (stage2_reason says why). The node table's immune_subtype is the subtype hint of the marker that named the cluster, not the cell's own, and is not carried."
      }
    }
